From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:58 +0000
Subject: Always show trivial subdomains in formatted URLs

url_formatter no longer removes trivial subdomains such as "www." from the
host when it formats a URL, even if the caller passes
kFormatUrlOmitTrivialSubdomains. This covers every caller, for example the
text of omnibox suggestions and the short origin labels that UrlFormatter
returns on Android, not only the address bar preference that this series
already changes. "www.example.com" and "example.com" are different hosts
that can have different owners, so hiding the prefix can mislead. Displayed
URLs become a few characters longer. GrapheneOS Vanadium uses the same
default.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 components/url_formatter/url_formatter.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/url_formatter/url_formatter.cc b/components/url_formatter/url_formatter.cc
--- a/components/url_formatter/url_formatter.cc
+++ b/components/url_formatter/url_formatter.cc
@@ -598,6 +598,8 @@ std::u16string FormatUrlWithAdjustments(
     base::OffsetAdjuster::Adjustments* adjustments) {
   DCHECK(adjustments);
   adjustments->clear();
+  // A subdomain such as "www." is part of the host, so it is always shown.
+  format_types &= ~kFormatUrlOmitTrivialSubdomains;
   url::Parsed parsed_temp;
   if (!new_parsed) {
     new_parsed = &parsed_temp;
--
